  ▐ aura  Done. The fix is in the working tree, verified on disk (read of `django/db/models/sql/query.py:1339-1342` shows the change), and the repro script is removed.

## What the bug was
`Query.build_where()` (used by `CheckConstraint._get_check_sql`) calls `_add_q(..., simple_col=True)` so check-constraint SQL gets `SimpleCol` — bare column names, required because check constraints can't use qualified `"table"."column"` names on SQLite/Oracle. But in `_add_q`, the **recursive call for nested `Q` children dropped `simple_col`**, so it defaulted to `False`. Any condition nested under an OR/AND combination then built fully-qualified `Col` objects — exactly the "OR and AND combined" case in the issue.

## The fix (one line, source only, no tests touched, not committed)
`django/db/models/sql/query.py`, `_add_q` — pass `simple_col` down the recursion:
```python
child_clause, needed_inner = self._add_q(
    child, used_aliases, branch_negated,
    current_negated, allow_joins, split_subq,
    simple_col=simple_col)
```

## Evidence
